issing fields.\n\n`summarize()` now only loops over orders and keeps the running totals. It calls these helpers:\n- **`_price_items`:** prices an order's items, counts units per SKU, and reports bad items.\n- **`_discount`:** applies the coupon rules.\n- **`_shipping`:** works out the shipping fee.\n- **`_order_total`:** combines discount, tax and shipping into a rounded total.\n- **`_record_customer`:** adds the total to the customer's running entry.\n- **`_top_sku` and `_best_customer`:** pick the top SKU and the best customer.\n- **`_build_report`:** assembles the final dict.\n\nEvery function is well under 30 lines, and I used only the standard library.\n\nI kept two oddities from the original on purpose. Units from valid items still count toward the top SKU even if a strict order is later skipped. Cancelled orders are counted in `status_counts` but are skipped for everything else.","ttft_ms":2032,"type":"result","duration_ms":25541,"uuid":"5287f425-d190-49e1-9fa7-8451f152a377","ttft_stream_ms":1387,"time_to_request_ms":47,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":12,"system_prompt":10,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":5,"input_hooks":1,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":2,"engine_pickup":1,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":6,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":2,"request_build":4},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":0,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":82,"time_to_request_major_faults":1,"first_content_frame_ms":1387,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
